{
  "requirement": "Each bundled skill MUST open, before any other section, with its workflow as ordered steps. Each bundled skill, recognized by its front matter, is a site:\n\n:::{sites} skills\n```yaml\nlanguage: markdown\npaths: [assets/skills]\nrule:\n  kind: minus_metadata\nmatch:\n  - \"---\\nname: example\\n---\\n\\n# Example\\n\"\nno_match:\n  - \"# Example\\n\"\n```\n:::",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Site query.** The `skills` query (`kind: minus_metadata`, markdown, `paths: [assets/skills]`) matches exactly five files. They are `assets/skills/{habeas,habeas-requirements,habeas-evidence,habeas-bootstrap-requirements,habeas-refactor}/SKILL.md`.\n\n- A regex search for files that begin with `---\\nname:` found the same five and no others.\n- The `references/*.md` files have no front matter, so they are correctly not sites.\n- The `SKILLS` constant in `tests/authoring_cli.rs` lists the same five skills.\n- The match snippet has front matter and the no_match snippet has none. Together they show what the query selects and what it leaves out.\n- I found no missed places and no out-of-scope selections.\n\n**Obligations.** The requirement has one obligation per site: the skill opens, before any other section, with its workflow as ordered steps. The whole-file sites each uphold this on their own. No part of it is left to specific code.\n\n**Test.** `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[bundled_skills_open_with_their_workflow_as_ordered_steps]` is marked `{test}` and loops over all five skills.\n\n- It asserts that the first `## ` line of each `SKILL.md` is `## Workflow`. That checks that the workflow section comes before any other section.\n- The outline search shows every skill has `# Title`, then `## Workflow`, then the other sections. A skill with another section first would fail this assertion.\n- It reads the steps through the helper `workflow_steps`, which parses the `- [ ] N. text` lines of the Workflow section up to the next `## `.\n- It asserts at least two steps. It also asserts the numbers equal `1..=n`, which checks that the steps are ordered and sequential.\n\nThe test checks the heading position, the presence of steps, and their ordering for every site. I found no scenario the requirement names that the test leaves out.",
  "references": "bdd2c44e881310eaa176cac0bc633689971a0bf7aef8b3b2d4d14ac7fe919877",
  "inputs": [
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.cli.skill_conventions.workflow",
      "matches": [
